      },
      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "An optimizer update changes Megatron's actor weights. SGLang needs a separate synchronization step before sampling from that policy. Our full-disk trace first publishes a versioned weight artifact and pulls it to the destination. During those preparation stages, the old policy remains live.\n",
          "start": 0.4,
          "end": 18.808,
          "duration": 18.408,
          "until": 19.408
        },
        {
          "say": "Pause admissions at the live transition, flush incompatible cached state, and reload the prepared artifact. Follow the clock: a published version and a loaded serving version are different events. The displayed engine version advances only after this supplied reload finishes successfully.\n",
          "start": 19.408,
          "end": 37.288,
          "duration": 17.88,
          "until": 37.888000000000005
        },
        {
          "say": "Our supplied outcome reports a successful reload and a separate version check matching the expected policy. Those receipts permit admissions to resume. Other paths have different carriers and ordering: colocated full updates can use tensor handles, while non-colocated full updates can broadcast through NCCL. A weight export also needs explicit retention and durable storage if it will be used for recovery.\n",
          "start": 37.888000000000005,
          "end": 62.824000000000005,
          "duration": 24.936,
          "until": 63.42400000000001
        }
      ],
